course: dictionary
lesson: 15401
title: Who speaks for the group?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A spokesman is a person chosen to speak for a whole group, so that everyone's message comes from one voice. Look for clues like «for» and the name of the group, such as the police, a government, or a team.
explain: «The police spokesman said the road would close at noon.» The word spokesman tells you that the police chose one person to speak, so this news is official. Ask yourself: who is speaking, and who are they speaking for?
explain: Spokeswoman and spokesperson are other words for the same job. You will often see the word in the news, where a spokesman for a company or government answers questions.
fact: «Spokesman» means a person chosen to speak officially for a group, company, team or government.
fact: «Spokesmen» is the plural, meaning more than one spokesman.
fact: «Spokeswoman» and «spokesperson» mean the same job as spokesman.
fact: You will often hear «a spokesman for the police said…» on the news, which tells you the information is official.
fact: In school, a class may choose a spokesperson to speak to the head teacher on behalf of everyone.
exercise: «The school spokesman read the news to the whole assembly.» What is a spokesman? | A child who is always late | A person who cleans the classrooms | *A person chosen to speak for a group | A type of bird
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means the same job as spokesman: «The club chose Priya as its spokesperson.» | *spokesperson | club | Priya | chose
exercise: «A government spokeswoman answered questions on the news tonight.» Who answered the questions? | A famous singer on holiday | *A person speaking officially for the government | A class of children on a school trip | The head teacher's dog
test: What is the plural of spokesman? | spokesmans | spokesmanes | spokesman-es | *spokesmen
test: «The team asked Sam to be their spokesperson at the prize-giving.» What does spokesperson mean here? | The person who made the trophy | *The person chosen to speak for the team | The person who ran the fastest | The person who won the most points
exam: «The police spokesman said no one was hurt.» What does this sentence tell you? | The police were hungry | The police lost their way | Nobody was hurt because the police were silly | *The police chose one person to give official news
